WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540
If there is one thing to remember, it's this:

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:07.320
Fire fades, and it's inevitable and natural for the world to return to dark.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.820
The future is dark, but it was not always this way.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.980
Let's go back to where there was a flame.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.920
The Hero has made it to the Kiln,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.500
where the First Flame was found, thrived, faded and was kindled again.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.100
The Hero descends to kill the god who kindled that flame.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.820
This god is a shell now, a husk.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.640
He's lost his kingdom, his knights, his wife, children, and friends.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.020
But even with nothing left, he sacrificed himself to keep the Dark at bay.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.980
This is the story of a man who fought against the inevitable.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.400
In the beginning, there were two planes of existence:

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.020
There was the Above, and the Below.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.880
Above was grey, with Dragons who had existed forever.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.420
Nothing changed, nothing progressed and nothing lived or died.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.200
I think of the below as dark, although it probably was nothing of the sort.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.520
How can darkness exist without light ?

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.760
But that was about to change,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.240
because when the Flame came, it created Disparity.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.660
Now there was Light and Dark, and the Light illuminated the creatures who were hiding.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.360
These creatures emerged to inspect the Flame,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.540
and these were the ones who would become known as Giants.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.300
For within the Flame was great power, and four Giants claimed this power.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.000
They claimed it, and it shaped them.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.580
Nito came to embody Death,

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.780
the Witch of Izalith represented Life,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.560
Lord Gwyn stood for the Light and the Pygmy kept his Dark Soul a secret.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.520
Gwyn decreed that the Flame was more powerful than the grey existence up above,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.040
and the Giants declared war on the Dragons to claim the surface.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.660
Alas, the Dragons were immortal and many knights of Gwyn fell,

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.080
but there was one Dragon who betrayed his own.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.080
Seath the Scaleless,

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.480
born without the stone scales of immortality, told the Dragons' weakness to Gwyn.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.960
The stone scales were the secret to their immortality, and the lightning was their weakness.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:03.360
So Gwyn and his knights fashioned bolts of lightning to peel apart their stone scales,

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.340
Nito unleashed disease on their exposed flesh,

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.320
and the Witch of Izalith and her followers used fire sorceries to burn their homes,

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.140
the arch-trees, to ash.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.200
And the Dragons were no more.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.780
And so, the Age of Fire was born,

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.740
and the Giants began their own story.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.120
But since this is a story about Light,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.440
it is also a story about Dark.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.880
For it is inevitable that one day, the Flame will fade,

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.980
and only Dark will remain.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.440
Seath was granted three rewards:

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.520
He received a piece of Gwyn's Lord Soul,

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.720
a dukedom in Gwyn's kingdom, and his own research facility to discover immortality,

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.660
something he never would have had with the Dragons around.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.860
The Age of Fire had changed the shape of the world.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.000
Gwyn's kingdom grew during the Age of Fire,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.520
and the lands outside assumedly looked to Lordran as their capital city.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.140
Anor Londo was built close to the sun,

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.160
and eventually smaller towns and cities grew to surround it.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.860
The Giants became the royalty and the gods,

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:05.220
and Humanity spread, worshiping those more powerful than them.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.560
Gwyn himself had a wife whose name is not known,

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.740
and by her, he had three children.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.860
His firstborn was the God of War,

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.540
who formed the Warriors of Sunlight.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.120
However, he lost the annals, which were historical records.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.860
Gwyn decreed that his son would share the same fate,

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.740
and all record of the firstborn was stripped from the land.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.460
Gwyn's secondborn, Gwynevere, was well-loved

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.960
with her own statues and covenant: The Princess's Guard.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.180
The third of birth was Gwyndolin, who was born frail and deformed.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:36.700
He was raised as a daughter since he was proficient at moonlight magic,

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.740
which is considered a female trait.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:42.460
His existence was hidden, and his covenant, the Blade of the Darkmoons,

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:45.680
hunt down sinners and protect the illusion of power in Anor Londo.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.140
For hundreds of years, the Lords prospered.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.580
But everything ends.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:58.200
Locked away in his archives, Seath is desperately searching for the secret to immortality.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.480
The six-eyed channelers read for him,

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.580
and search the world for test subjects.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.360
These test subjects are locked away in crystal golems

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.380
for transportation back to the archives,

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.860
where they become the subject of his experiments.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.860
At the base of the prison there are Pisacas,

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.540
twisted monsters created from captured maidens.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.220
If you listen carefully, you can hear them crying.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.220
At some point, the knowledge in the archives sends Seath mad.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.920
It's impossible to know whether he was insane before

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.940
or after his experiments on the maidens.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.700
But one way or another,

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:34.700
Gwyn turns a blind eye to the happenings in the archives.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.260
Perhaps it was this that led to the rebellion against the Gods.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.420
In the war against the Dragons,

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.380
Lord Gwyn had a friend and compatriot named Havel the Rock,

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.480
who was the sworn enemy of magic and Seath the Scaleless.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.920
After the war, Gwyn granted Seath dukedom and a part of his own soul.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.140
Perhaps Havel was bitter at Gwyn's preference for Seath

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.220
since he started to collect items capable of killing the Gods.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.000
Hidden in his basement in Anor Londo,

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:02.420
there is an Occult club.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.820
Items of the Occult can kill the Gods,

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.020
and are rightly feared.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.340
Havel was also a bishop of the Church,

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.640
who knew the whereabouts of the Dark Ember.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.800
Lastly, the Effigy Shield states

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.440
that there was once an ill-fated plot to destroy the Gods.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:16.900
Ill-fated,

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.640
because the attempt failed.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.640
Among the royalty, there are rumors of a hero

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.900
locked away in a stern cell by a dear friend.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.960
They say he was locked away for his own good,

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.980
which led many to believe that the man inside had gone Hollow.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:32.540
Havel helped Gwyn win his throne,

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.900
but met with the fate of the Undead and was

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.060
kept in a cell so he could not harm others.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.300
That's what they would have you believe.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.840
But what if Gwyn learned of Havel's plan

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:42.840
to kill the Gods?

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.840
Perhaps Havel was not Hollow when he was locked away.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.540
Perhaps he was locked away for the good of the realm,

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.840
and left Hollow in the middle of an area overrun by Hollows.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.060
Gwyn would have locked his friend away

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:55.980
for the greater good,

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:57.840
but was it the right thing to do?

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.620
This marks the peak of the Age of Fire,

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.280
and the Darkness is looming.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:04.880
Soon, Gwyn will need all the friends he can get.

